      "body": "## Motivation\n\nFixes #43352. On the CPU path, `runai_safetensors_weights_iterator` yields views into the Run:ai streamer's staging buffers, which the streamer reuses once its memory limit is reached. A weight loader that keeps a tensor until its counterpart arrives, such as the `nvfp4_online` MoE loader with its w1/w3 and FP8 weight/scale pairs, then reads bytes that belong to a later tensor.\n\n## Modifications\n\nOn the CPU path (`device == \"cpu\"`), the iterator copies each tensor before yielding it, so a yielded tensor owns its memory and stays valid however long a loader keeps it. vLLM's equivalent iterator copies every tensor it yields from the streamer in the same way.\n\nThe distributed path, which streams to the GPU, is unchanged. The cost is one host memory copy per tensor on the CPU path.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the code style guidelines.\n- [x] A streamed checkpoint that exceeds the streamer's memory limit yields every kept tensor unchanged with this change (most changed without it).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37916381621](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37916381621)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37916381086](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37916381086)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37916381903](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37916381903)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
