                  "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Avoid re-marking the owned CPU clone as a staging view**\n\nOn the CPU path this clone already breaks the staging-buffer alias, but the next line still applies `RUNAI_STREAMER_TENSOR_ATTR`. When loading DeepSeek/NVFP4 or GPT-OSS checkpoints, `_clone_if_runai_streamed_tensor` (`deepseek_common/deepseek_weight_loader.py:75-77`) and `_own_if_runai_streamed` (`gpt_oss.py:1365-1374`) react to that marker by making another full copy, so large paired MoE weights temporarily occupy the staging allocation plus two owned allocations and incur two host copies; this can exhaust host RAM in memory-limited streaming configurations. Mark only tensors that still alias streamer storage, or otherwise distinguish this already-owned clone for those consumers.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.",
