      "changes": 6,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/contents/python%2Fsglang%2Fsrt%2Fmodel_loader%2Fweight_utils.py?ref=13875f7f97be765863e60b852ebf1e971c509e2e",
      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": "python/sglang/srt/model_loader/weight_utils.py",
      "patch": "@@ -1619,6 +1619,12 @@ def runai_safetensors_weights_iterator(\n         )\n \n         for name, tensor in tensor_iter:\n+            if device == \"cpu\":\n+                # On the CPU path the streamer yields views into its staging\n+                # buffers, which it reuses once its memory limit is reached. A\n+                # loader that keeps a tensor until its counterpart arrives (MoE\n+                # experts, online quantization) would read later tensors' bytes.\n+                tensor = tensor.clone()\n             setattr(tensor, RUNAI_STREAMER_TENSOR_ATTR, True)\n             yield name, tensor\n ",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/raw/13875f7f97be765863e60b852ebf1e971c509e2e/python%2Fsglang%2Fsrt%2Fmodel_loader%2Fweight_utils.py",
      "sha": "dd9aa9ca4e774839dd11b8f5b8c81addb5692a0a",
      "status": "modified"
    }
  ],
  "inline_comments": [
    {
      "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Avoid re-marking the owned CPU clone as a staging view**\n\nOn the CPU path this clone already breaks the staging-buffer alias, but the next line still applies `RUNAI_STREAMER_TENSOR_ATTR`. When loading DeepSeek/NVFP4 or GPT-OSS checkpoints, `_clone_if_runai_streamed_tensor` (`deepseek_common/deepseek_weight_loader.py:75-77`) and `_own_if_runai_streamed` (`gpt_oss.py:1365-1374`) react to that marker by making another full copy, so large paired MoE weights temporarily occupy the staging allocation plus two owned allocations and incur two host copies; this can exhaust host RAM in memory-limited streaming configurations. Mark only tensors that still alias streamer storage, or otherwise distinguish this already-owned clone for those consumers.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-09T10:18:08Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -1619,6 +1619,12 @@ def runai_safetensors_weights_iterator(\n         )\n \n         for name, tensor in tensor_iter:\n+            if device == \"cpu\":\n+                # On the CPU path the streamer yields views into its staging\n+                # buffers, which it reuses once its memory limit is reached. A\n+                # loader that keeps a tensor until its counterpart arrives (MoE\n+                # experts, online quantization) would read later tensors' bytes.\n+                tensor = tensor.clone()",
